      "why": "Pipelined gives 1 result/cycle, which is critical for the bursty Poisson system constraint (p99 <= 0.4us) and throughput >= 2 Msps. With 1 result/cycle, a burst of 8 requests takes 8 cycles to drain. At Fmax ~200MHz (5ns/cycle), 8 cycles = 40ns, well within 0.4us. The main trade-off is accuracy vs area: n_iter and data_width control max_abs_err, while angle_guard and frac_guard add area. We need max_abs_err <= 2^-10 = 0.000976562. For CORDIC, error ~ 2^-(n_iter + data_width - 2) roughly, so n_iter=12-16 with data_width=12-16 should suffice. Keeping data_width modest (12-16) minimizes LUTs+FFs. angle_guard and frac_guard in 0-2 keep area low while providing some margin. This family is the primary candidate for the Pareto front."
